	<h3 id="comments">2 Memories for &#8220;Hakim Harry Williams&#8221;</h3> 

	<ol class="commentlist">
						<li class="alt" id="comment-4276">
			<div class="cmtinfo"><em> on 26 Mar 2010 at 9:19 am</em><small class="commentmetadata"><a href="index.html%3Fp=610#comment-4276" title=""><span class="commentnum">1</span></a></small><cite><a href='http://ismailabushams.blogspot.com/' rel='external nofollow' class='url'>Isma'il Martens</a></cite></div>
						
			<p>I met Hakim at the Abode , during my first stay there (1989) and later again at my return from 1996 till 2001<br />
My most vivid memory was when my son Connor exclaimed in the Abode dining room &#8221; Dad you are weird &#8221; and Hakim replied beside me &#8221; Better weird than boring &#8221; &#8230;<br />
Hakim studied under Timothy Leary and could tell  great stories ..</p>
			
		</li>

	
					<li class="" id="comment-14261">
			<div class="cmtinfo"><em> on 21 Feb 2013 at 1:57 am</em><small class="commentmetadata"><a href="index.html%3Fp=610#comment-14261" title=""><span class="commentnum">2</span></a></small><cite>Mariel Walters</cite></div>
						
			<p>I was friends with Hakim both in Atlanta and at the Abode.  He was intelligent, kind and good hearted, and I enjoyed his company.  I&#8217;m glad he&#8217;s at peace.</p>
			
		</li>

	
	
	</ol>

